WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.440
How much extra space, beyond the length of your own car,

00:03.720 --> 00:07.040
do you actually need to parallel park in one smooth sweep?

00:07.860 --> 00:10.040
Nobody enjoys shuffling back and forth,

00:10.460 --> 00:13.460
inching closer to the curb a few centimeters at a time.

00:14.140 --> 00:17.440
Mathematician Simon Blackburn solved the exact geometry.

00:17.880 --> 00:21.260
For a typical car with a turning radius of 5.4 meters,

00:21.740 --> 00:26.400
a wheelbase of 2.6 meters, and a front overhang of 1.3 meters,

00:26.400 --> 00:29.740
parking behind a car that is 1.7 meters wide,

00:30.300 --> 00:32.860
his formula gives a surprisingly tight answer,

00:33.320 --> 00:37.400
just 1.43 meters of extra room, less than 5 feet.

00:37.980 --> 00:41.700
Anything tighter than that, and geometry forces you to start shuffling.

